# What never leaves this machine when `railway up` uploads the build
# context.
#
# .gitignore already covers `.env` and `.env*.local`, and the CLI honours
# it, so today nothing secret is sent. This file exists because that is a
# coincidence of two patterns rather than a rule: `.env.production` and
# `.env.staging` match neither, and would be uploaded by whoever adds one.
# The runner's four secrets are handed to it by Railway at run time, so no
# env file ever needs to travel with the source.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Not part of the worker, and the largest things here. The runner renders
# nothing and builds no templates; see the Dockerfile for what it copies.
node_modules
.next
public
components
hooks
sandbox
tests
bench
scratchpad
